# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when cloned on Windows. Git's default
# there is core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites them to CRLF on checkout — and a
# shell then fails on the trailing \r with an error that names a line rather
# than the cause ("$'\r': command not found"). copy-dist.sh runs as
# beforeBuildCommand, so this breaks the desktop build itself, not just tooling.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The frontend is served byte-for-byte to a webview; keep it stable across
# platforms so a Windows checkout builds the same bytes a mac one does.
*.js  text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pptx binary
